WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.634
-Thank you for being here, bud.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:04.901
-You look great, pal.
-You too.

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.234
-I want to talk to you
about this.

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:08.033
"Rolling Stone" magazine came
out with a list of

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.968
the greatest TV
shows of all time.

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:16.167
And number 1 on the list,
"The Sopranos."

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:18.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:24.467
How does that feel?
How does it feel to be --

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:28.133
-It's very, very cool.
It's been interesting.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.100
Lately, a lot of younger people

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.267
are getting turned on to
"The Sopranos."

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.434
-Yeah.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:35.167
-Now it's Halloween time,
I get on my Instagram --

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.901
a lot of my followers
send me pictures of them

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:40.667
in their
Christopher Moltisanti costume.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.434
-Yeah.
-Christopher and Adriana.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:43.934
-Yeah, and you did this --
So, all these --

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:45.434
like hundreds of people,
thousands of people --

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:49.000
-I get lots and then I pick my
favorites and then I post them.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.367
And all kinds of people.
It's really fun.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.634
A lot of young people,
though, predominantly, yeah.

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:56.634
-Is it wild to see people
that weren't alive

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:59.801
when the show came out,
they'll be giant fans of yours?

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:02.367
-It's very, very wild.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:05.601
I was in -- I became aware of it
a couple years ago.

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:08.100
I was in Central Park
shooting something,

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.400
and this kid from Scotland
comes up to me.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.968
He was like 18.
He was with his father.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:13.167
They were visiting New York.

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.000
And he pulls up his pant leg,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.300
and on his calf
is a tattoo of me.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.300
And I was -- You know, it was a
little bit -- a little scary.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.400
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.133
-But he was
cool and really nice.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:28.267
And it just made me aware that,

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:31.000
wow, this whole new generation
of young people

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.567
have been turned on to the show
and really, really liking it.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:33.868
-And into it.

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:36.767
Yeah, I also think, you know,
there was lockdown,

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:38.968
and everyone was looking
for things to do and watch.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:41.934
And everyone rewatched that
or, if they hadn't seen it,

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.234
watched "The Sopranos."

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:45.534
And you go, "This actually
is a phenomenal show.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:47.334
It holds up even right now."

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:50.434
And it's in -- How many
years ago did it start?

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.868
-It started --
It went on the air in '99.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.501
-'99.
-Yeah. It's a long time ago.

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:55.567
-That doesn't seem like that.
Yeah.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:58.167
-It went off the air
15 years ago.

00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:00.400
-Well, your podcast is
very great, too.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.767
You and Steve Schirripa.
-Schirripa.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.801
We did an episode-by-episode
rewatch of "The Sopranos."

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:07.300
And I had not seen it
since it went off the air.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.467
So during the pandemic,

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:11.901
I was watching it every week
and taking notes.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:14.434
-And you talk to everybody.
It's great interviews.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.934
Steve Schirripa, by the way,

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:17.901
used to book me
in comedy clubs before.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.067
-In Vegas, right?
-In Vegas.

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:20.133
-Yeah.
-That's correct.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.267
-That's right.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:22.734
-So, thank you, Steve,
for booking me,

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:24.734
'cause, yeah, it all led here.

00:02:24.734 --> 00:02:26.300
But it's a great thing.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.968
And there's always rumors
going around about, you know,

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:32.434
what was the end of
"The Sopranos"?

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:35.834
Did Tony get whacked?
I mean, you know.

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:38.267
-I still don't know.
-Come on!

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.000
-I do not know. I do not know.
-Come on!

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.067
-I've gone back and forth.
I thought I knew.

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:46.167
We had David Chase, the creator,
on the podcast three times,

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:49.200
and each time, there was little
tidbits and different things.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.601
I still don't know
what the hell happened.

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:51.834
I really don't.

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.901
And now I'm saying,
well, the end was the end.

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:56.167
It just ended,
and there's nothing after and --

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:57.234
-Yeah, the end was the end.

00:02:57.234 --> 00:02:58.801
It went to black,
and you kind of go...

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:02.000
-That's it.
-I kind of loved it. I loved it.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.300
I wasn't -- I'm one of the
people that are a fan of that.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.701
I thought it was great.

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:07.834
-You know, 15 years later,
we're still talking about it.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:09.000
-That's correct, yeah.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.400
-I guess that's a testament to
the, you know...

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.701
-Can't we call
David Chase and go,

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:13.868
"Hey, what's the deal, dude?"

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.667
-He'll never --
-Yeah, why would he?

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:17.067
-No. He's not
going to give it away.

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:18.634
-Do you stay in touch with him?
-Yeah.

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:19.868
-You do. Yeah.

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:22.634
-Yeah, we're writing
a movie together right now

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:25.167
for me and Steve Schirripa.

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.634
It's a mystery project.
-Wait. What?

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:29.834
-I can't talk about it
beyond that.

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:32.667
-You and Steve Schirripa
and David Chase?

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.200
-Yeah.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.400
-What are you talking --
You from "The Sopranos,"

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.734
Steve Schirripa
from "The Sopranos,"

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:40.901
David Chase from "The Sopranos"
are writing a movie?

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.067
And you can't talk about
what the movies about?

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:45.234
-David and I
are writing it together.

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:47.834
I can't say what it's about.

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:49.200
-I know, but --

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.300
-But when it comes out,
I'm gonna come here.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.701
-Okay. And talk about it.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:55.534
-Before anybody, I'm gonna come
here and talk about it.

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:57.601
-That's what I'm talking about.
That's what a friend is for.

00:03:57.601 --> 00:03:59.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:01.100
Thank you, buddy.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.267
Can we talk about
another great show?

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:06.234
Gosh, "White Lotus" was one of
the best things I've seen on TV.

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:08.334
I loved it so much.
I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:09.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.567
Mike White -- brilliant.
-Great.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:14.000
-Brilliantly acted.
The whole cast was all great.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.367
And now it's back for
a second installment.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:19.200
And I couldn't think of
a better person

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.300
to be in the cast than you.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.501
You're going to crush it.

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:22.968
How did you get involved with
"White Lotus"?

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:25.701
Can you describe what
this installment is about?

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:28.067
-This is --
takes place in Sicily.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.968
So we were in Sicily
four months,

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:31.767
which was a dream gig.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:33.567
I play a Hollywood producer
who is taking

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:36.767
his elderly father and his son
back to the old country

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:39.434
to retrace their family history.

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:42.934
But his marriage is
falling apart because of,

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:45.734
uh, sexual compulsion
and infidelity,

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:48.100
and his wife was supposed to
come and she didn't come.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.234
-Oh. She doesn't come to
The White Lotus?

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:53.000
-She doesn't come on vacation,
and I have to...

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:56.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:58.567
-That's not what -- No, hey,
that's not what he meant.

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.834
No, no. That's not what he --
Hey, hey, hey!

00:05:00.834 --> 00:05:01.934
That's not what you guys --

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.734
-You guys got your mind
in the gutter.

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:06.501
What the hell?

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:07.734
This is Jimmy Fallon,
for God's sakes.

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:08.868
-Thank you. Yeah, exactly.

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:10.300
Yeah, she doesn't travel
is what I meant.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.501
-She didn't travel.

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:14.434
She didn't accompany me
on the trip.

00:05:14.434 --> 00:05:16.534
-Your actual wife in real life
was with you, right?

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:18.534
-My wife was with me
the whole time.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:20.400
We were living and working in

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.467
the San Domenico Palace
in Taormina, Sicily,

00:05:22.467 --> 00:05:24.567
which was really fantastic --

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:27.300
until one night
when it wasn't fantastic,

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:32.434
because I had to shoot a scene
where my character

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:35.300
has a ménage à trois
in a hot tub

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.601
with two of
my great Italian co-stars,

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:39.801
Simona Tabasco
and Beatrice Granno,

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:41.767
who are fabulous actresses.

00:05:41.767 --> 00:05:45.200
But this is well
into the shoot, and it's --

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.567
You know,
we were friends by that point.

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:49.634
Now we've got to do this
sex scene in a tub.

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:52.267
So, we're doing it in
a big suite in the hotel,

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:55.367
and, you know, Mike's showing us
how it's going to work out.

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:56.701
And we go out to the patio.

00:05:56.701 --> 00:05:58.234
And "So, you'll
come out of the room

00:05:58.234 --> 00:05:59.501
and you'll go in the hot tub

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:02.601
and you'll take your clothes off
and you'll --" You know.

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:07.534
And I realize my wife is asleep
right above this hot --

00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:10.300
My room is right above
this hot tub.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.601
And if my wife --

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:13.267
Now, it's 2:00 in the morning
we go to shoot this.

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:15.501
If she wakes up, she's going to
look out the window

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:18.968
and see me pretty much naked
with my two Italian co-stars

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:21.367
messing around in a hot tub.

00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:24.367
And I go --
I'm like, "Oh, my God."

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:26.267
You know,
these scenes are awkward enough.

00:06:26.267 --> 00:06:27.701
-Sure, of course.

00:06:27.701 --> 00:06:30.767
-Now I'm worried about my wife
looking out the window.

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:32.734
And I get really --
So I'm trying to --

00:06:32.734 --> 00:06:35.367
I'm like,
"Mike, you know, hot tub?

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:39.634
I don't think Dominic's
a hot-tub guy, you know?"

00:06:39.634 --> 00:06:40.968
Why -- You know --

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:43.467
-I think he's a guy who
has sex with his clothes on.

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:46.767
-Look at that bed.
It's a big, king size --

00:06:46.767 --> 00:06:47.901
"No, no, no.

00:06:47.901 --> 00:06:49.167
You'll come out,
you'll get in the hot tub.

00:06:49.167 --> 00:06:50.901
It'll be fine. We'll go.
We'll put the music on."

00:06:50.901 --> 00:06:52.067
"Music?! No! What music?"

00:06:52.067 --> 00:06:54.334
"No, we got some house music.
The girl --"

00:06:54.334 --> 00:06:56.300
I said, "No, Mike.
We can't have music.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:58.467
There's people
sleeping right now.

00:06:58.467 --> 00:06:59.767
You can't have music."

00:06:59.767 --> 00:07:02.434
"We'll have music. Nobody cares.
It's just us in here."

00:07:02.434 --> 00:07:04.400
So, we do the scene.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.767
I'm, like, looking.

00:07:05.767 --> 00:07:07.467
You know, I'm thinking a lamp

00:07:07.467 --> 00:07:10.400
is going to come
sailing down from the window.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.767
Luckily, we got through it.

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:13.000
-Alright, good.
Good, good, good, good.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.868
-But then I'm thinking,
"Oh, wait.

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:16.234
She doesn't want to make a scene

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:17.567
because she knows
the crew by now.

00:07:17.567 --> 00:07:19.000
We've all been there together."

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.033
"She's waiting for
me to get back upstairs."

00:07:22.033 --> 00:07:24.300
Now it's 5:00 in the morning.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.567
I go in the room.
It's all quiet.

00:07:26.567 --> 00:07:28.934
You know, I go brush my teeth.
I'm coming to bed.

00:07:28.934 --> 00:07:33.334
She wakes up.
She goes, "How was it tonight?"

00:07:33.334 --> 00:07:37.133
And I'm like,
"Now, should I play this --"

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:38.734
I'm playing it cool.
"It was okay.

00:07:38.734 --> 00:07:40.934
It was okay."
"It was a long night?"

00:07:40.934 --> 00:07:42.968
"Yeah, you know.
It was kind of long."

00:07:42.968 --> 00:07:45.467
-It's work.
-"You tired?"

00:07:45.467 --> 00:07:47.367
"Yeah, I'm pretty tired."

00:07:47.367 --> 00:07:50.067
"Was it hard?"
"No. Absolutely not.

00:07:50.067 --> 00:07:53.234
I swear. I swear."
♪♪

00:07:53.234 --> 00:07:56.267
-It was not! Absolutely not!
-I swear on the kids.

00:07:56.267 --> 00:07:58.133
And she's like,
"What are you talking about?

00:07:58.133 --> 00:07:59.267
-Alright, we have a clip.

00:07:59.267 --> 00:08:01.133
It's not that clip,
but here's a clip.

00:08:01.133 --> 00:08:04.501
Here's Michael Imperioli in
"The White Lotus."

00:08:04.501 --> 00:08:05.734
Take a look at this.

00:08:05.734 --> 00:08:07.734
[ Knock on door ]

00:08:09.701 --> 00:08:10.734
-Hey.
-Hey.

00:08:10.734 --> 00:08:13.701
Um, Nonna, fell by the pool.
-What?

00:08:13.701 --> 00:08:16.934
-He's fine, um,
but I think he hit his head.

00:08:16.934 --> 00:08:19.601
He could have a concussion.

00:08:19.601 --> 00:08:22.000
I'm thinking someone
should sleep with him tonight,

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.234
keep an eye on him.

00:08:23.234 --> 00:08:26.701
-Yeah, good idea.
Um, we'll put him in your room.

00:08:26.701 --> 00:08:29.934
I got work stuff.
L.A. will still be up.

00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:31.567
I'm going to be
up and around all night,

00:08:31.567 --> 00:08:35.234
so let's just, uh -- We'll put
him in your room, okay?

00:08:35.234 --> 00:08:36.968
-[ Sighs ] Okay.

00:08:36.968 --> 00:08:38.267
-Anything else?
-No.

00:08:38.267 --> 00:08:41.067
-What do you say?
Dinner at 8:00?

00:08:41.067 --> 00:08:42.901
-Yeah, sure.

00:08:42.901 --> 00:08:44.167
-Alright.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:49.267
-Yeah, that settles it.
"He goes in your room."

00:08:49.267 --> 00:08:51.634
-And they know now
what's going to happen.

00:08:51.634 --> 00:08:52.968
-What's going to happen.

00:08:52.968 --> 00:08:54.300
I do want to quickly say,

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.434
congrats on your band,
by the way, Zopa, right here.

00:08:57.434 --> 00:08:59.167
And you're currently --
You're playing right now.

00:08:59.167 --> 00:09:00.534
You're on tour?

00:09:00.534 --> 00:09:03.334
-We're doing a show in
Boston and New York in December.

00:09:03.334 --> 00:09:04.968
Yeah, two shows coming up.

00:09:04.968 --> 00:09:06.834
-Congrats on that.
This is getting great reviews.

00:09:06.834 --> 00:09:08.501
-Thank you.
-Thanks for coming by, buddy.

00:09:08.501 --> 00:09:10.133
Michael Imperioli.

00:09:10.133 --> 00:09:12.767
"The White Lotus" returns
with a second installment

00:09:12.767 --> 00:09:16.167
this Sunday at 9:00 p.m.
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:09:16.167 --> 00:09:18.167
We'll be right back with a
performance from Tegan and Sara.

00:09:18.167 --> 00:09:19.300
Stick around.

